# ========== Compression Modulus Simulation — Plate-Driven (Isotropic) ==========
# Input: isolated gel WITH six plates attached (from add_more_plates_to_gel.ipynb).
# Atom types: 1=polymer, 2=crosslinker, 3=solvent, 4=plate
# Bond types:  1=FENE (polymer-polymer only; plates interact via WCA, no bonds)
#
# Compression method: fix move linear on all six plate groups simultaneously.
#   Top   plate (+z face): vz = -vcompress_z   Bot   plate (-z face): vz = +vcompress_z
#   Front plate (+y face): vy = -vcompress_y   Back  plate (-y face): vy = +vcompress_y
#   Right plate (+x face): vx = -vcompress_x   Left  plate (-x face): vx = +vcompress_x
#   Plates move only along their normal axis → isotropic compression.
#   Plate atoms are bonded (harmonic) to surface polymer → gel compresses internally.
#   No direct force on FENE bonds; harmonic bonds transmit load at each face safely.
#
# Plate-plate interactions disabled (neigh_modify exclude type 4 4) to prevent
# spurious cross-face forces between the six independent plate molecules.
#
# Why NOT fix deform (box compression):
#   fix deform rescales ALL atom positions, which conflicts with the plate-polymer
#   harmonic bonds and risks FENE failure at the driven surfaces.
#   Plate-driven compression keeps the box fixed; plates mechanically transmit
#   the load to the gel through harmonic bonds (same logic as shear_slab).
#
# Phases:  (equilibration ported from slab_with_flow.lmp — Langevin beats FENE heating)
#   0.  NVT settle (nsteps_phase0) — fixed box, all 6 plates frozen (fix move 0 0 0)
#   0.5 Langevin+NPH iso (nsteps_npt) — find equilibrium box volume at P = P_target;
#       plates released to nve+setforce so they scale isotropically with the box
#   1b. NVT (nsteps_equil) — relax internal stresses at NPH-final volume, plates frozen
#   0/3 ε_vol = 0 REFERENCE — plates frozen, NVT hold of nsteps_ref steps with the
#       same averaging as a stage hold, writing stress_tensor_{polymer,solvent}_ref_*.
#       Gives a MEASURED P'_net at zero strain instead of the assumed zero that
#       K_single would otherwise use. (Ported from slab_with_flow's ref_ block.)
#   2/3 STAGED (slope method, 3 stages) — for each of 3 cumulative VOLUMETRIC
#       strain targets (compress_strain_vol = 0.015, 0.030, 0.045):
#         (a) drive all 6 plates inward (gel on Langevin+NVE) until
#             compress_strain_vol reaches that stage's target (checked every
#             halt_freq steps — see the halt_freq note in PARAMETERS)
#         (b) freeze all 6 plates, hold NVT for ~nsteps steps (per-stage
#             equilibration length — see NOTE below) so the solvent can
#             redistribute/drain before anything is measured
#         (c) average the equilibrated stress tensor over that hold
#       Stress/strain data from all 3 stages accumulate into the SAME output
#       files (stage 1 creates them, stages 2-3 append), so downstream
#       analysis can read one continuous file per quantity and fit ΔP'_net
#       vs ε_vol across the 3 equilibrated points (the slope = K), rather
#       than trusting a single point.
#       All 3 stages lie inside the estimated linear-elastic window (see STAGE
#       TARGETS in PARAMETERS for the linearity table), so this ladder measures
#       the linear-elastic K only — the deliberately-nonlinear ε_vol = 0.060
#       and 0.120 rungs that probed strain stiffening have been removed.
#
#   NOTE on drainage / hold length: nsteps (below) means the length of
#   EACH of the 3 equilibration holds, not one single Phase-3 run. No
#   cooperative diffusivity (D_c) value was available when this was written,
#   so nsteps is NOT yet derived from τ ~ L_gel²/D_c — it is passed through
#   unchanged from the previous single-point launch command as a starting
#   point, not a validated drainage time. Before trusting the fitted slope:
#   pull D_c from compression_analysis.ipynb, compute τ = L_gel²/D_c, and
#   confirm nsteps ≳ a few τ. Also check drainage empirically —
#   stress_tensor_solvent_*.dat and stress_profile_z_solvent_*.dat are written
#   continuously through the whole staged run, so you can plot the solvent
#   stress within each stage's hold window and confirm it has actually
#   plateaued (not still drifting) before the next compression stage begins.
#   If any stage looks undrained, increase nsteps and rerun.
#
#   NOTE on epoch alignment (why the holds do NOT run exactly `nsteps`):
#   each hold's `run` is padded to end ON an nfreq_stress boundary via the
#   hold_steps variable defined at each stage. This is REQUIRED, not cosmetic.
#   fix ave/chunk (ave = one, the default) locks its compute chunk/atom at the
#   first sample of each Nfreq epoch and only releases the lock when that epoch
#   COMPLETES; FixAveChunk's destructor unlocks only for ave = running/window,
#   so `unfix` on a mid-epoch fix leaves the chunk compute locked by a deleted
#   fix. The next stage's fix ave/chunk then requests a different lock window
#   and LAMMPS aborts with:
#       ERROR: Two fix commands using same compute chunk/atom command in
#              incompatible ways (src/compute_chunk_atom.cpp:680)
#   That check is literally `startstep != lockstart || stopstep != lockstop`.
#   Ending each hold on an epoch boundary lets end_of_step() call unlock()
#   naturally, so the following unfix sees lockfix == nullptr.
#   Same failure and same remedy as the pre-roll alignment block in
#   slab_with_flow.lmp (see its notes around the ref_ fix teardown).
#   Consequence: each hold runs between nsteps and nsteps+nfreq_stress-1 steps
#   (<= ~10% longer than requested), never fewer than nsteps.
#
#   NOTE on bulk region: the poly_bulk/solv_bulk groups (3σ near-plate
#   exclusion) are defined ONCE, right after Phase 1b, using the
#   PRE-compression gel geometry — the same specific atoms are tracked
#   through all 3 stages (Lagrangian), rather than re-snapshotting which
#   atoms fall in the exclusion box after each stage's compression (which
#   the original single-point script never had to do, and which would
#   require deleting/redefining LAMMPS regions and computes mid-run — avoided
#   here for robustness since it can't be tested against a running LAMMPS
#   instance in this environment). Flag if you'd rather have per-stage
#   regrouping; it's a bigger change and worth doing deliberately, not as a
#   silent default.
#
# Plate mol IDs (assigned by add_more_plates_to_gel.ipynb):
#   top   = max_mol_gel + 1      bot   = max_mol_gel + 2
#   front = max_mol_gel + 3      back  = max_mol_gel + 4
#   right = max_mol_gel + 5      left  = max_mol_gel + 6
# These are resolved at runtime via compute reduce max mol on the gel group.
# (Spatial region grouping fails because right/left plates span the full y-range,
#  overlapping with the y-extent of front/back plates.)
#
# Outputs (all continuous across the whole staged run, Phase 0 -> Stage 3 hold,
#          unless noted; compress_strain_vol will show a 3-step staircase):
#   stress_data/bulk_modulus_plot_data_*.dat   step  sigP_xx/yy/zz/xy/zx/yz  Pi  V_gel_rg  lx/ly/lz_rg
#                                               (whole-polymer, Rg-normalised; osmotic path — NOT for K)
#   stress_data/plate_force_*.dat              step  {top,bot,front,back,right,left}_{fx,fy,fz}
#                                               (net pairwise force on each plate; continuous from the
#                                                point the six plates are individually resolved onward)
#   stress_data/stress_tensor_{polymer,solvent}_ref_*.dat
#                                               ε_vol = 0 baseline (Stage 0), same columns/averaging
#                                               as the staged files below; own file, not appended
#   stress_data/stress_tensor_polymer_*.dat    6-component polymer stress, EQUILIBRATED-HOLD windows only
#                                               (3 stages appended into one file — this is the K data)
#   stress_data/stress_tensor_solvent_*.dat    6-component solvent stress, EQUILIBRATED-HOLD windows only
#                                               (same 3-stage append; use for baseline + drainage check)
#   stress_data/stress_profile_z_polymer_*.dat z-binned polymer stress, EQUILIBRATED-HOLD windows only
#   stress_data/stress_profile_z_solvent_*.dat z-binned solvent stress, EQUILIBRATED-HOLD windows only
#   stress_data/compress_strain_*.dat          step  gap_z_0  gap_z  strain_z  strain_vol (staircase, all stages)
#   volume_data/gel_dimensions_rg_*.dat        Rg-based gel dimensions (continuous, all stages)
#   volume_data/box_dimensions_*.dat           box dims vs step (continuous, all stages)
#   volume_data/polymer_com_*.dat              polymer COM vs step (continuous, all stages)


# ==========================================================================
#                              PARAMETERS
# ==========================================================================

variable sigma          equal 1.0
variable temp_target    equal 1.0
variable P_target       equal 1.5
variable timestep_prod  equal 0.005

# ── STAGE TARGETS: VOLUMETRIC strain (NOT per-axis) ───────────────────────────
# The ladder is expressed in compress_strain_vol, because that is the strain K
# is defined against (K = dP'_net/dε_vol) and the quantity bulk_modulus_
# analysis.ipynb fits. Compression here is ISOTROPIC (all six plates move, all
# three axes strain equally), so ε_vol = 1-(1-ε_axis)^3 ≈ 3·ε_axis — a per-axis
# ladder is ~3x deeper than it looks, which is how the previous 0.02..0.10
# per-axis ladder ended up spanning ε_vol = 0.068..0.279.
#
# Linear-elastic window: for a swollen network in athermal solvent Π ~ φ^(9/4)
# with φ = φ0/(1-ε_vol), so P'_net(ε_vol) deviates from a straight line by
#   ε_vol :  0.015   0.030   0.045
#   dev   :   2.5%    5.1%    7.8%
# All three stages sit inside that window, so the 3-point fit (plus the
# measured ε_vol = 0 origin) gives the linear-elastic K. Per-axis equivalents
# (for reference only): 0.0050  0.0101  0.0152
# NOTE: this window is a SCALING ESTIMATE, not a measurement. Collinearity of
# the 3 points is the check that the ladder stayed inside it. The deeper
# ε_vol = 0.060 / 0.120 rungs (which deliberately probed strain stiffening)
# have been removed — add them back if K(ε) is wanted.
variable stage1_target equal 0.015
variable stage2_target equal 0.030
variable stage3_target equal 0.045

# Deepest volumetric strain, and its per-axis equivalent.
# target_strain_comp is used ONLY to set the plate ramp velocity below; the
# halt conditions all key off compress_strain_vol.
#   ε_axis = 1 - (1-ε_vol)^(1/3)
variable target_strain_vol  equal ${stage3_target}
variable target_strain_comp equal 1.0-(1.0-${target_strain_vol})^(1.0/3.0)

# Phase lengths
variable nsteps_phase0        equal 50000    # Phase 0:   NVT settle at fixed box (new; = old nsteps_npt)
variable nsteps_npt           equal 50000    # Phase 0.5: Langevin+NPH — find equilibrium volume at P_target
variable nsteps_equil         equal 50000    # Phase 1b:  NVT — equilibrate at NPH-final volume
variable nsteps_ref           equal 100000   # Stage 0:   ε_vol = 0 reference hold (own file, own length)
# Ramp velocity reference. vcompress is set so the plates cover the FULL ladder
# (0 -> target_strain_vol = 0.045) in nsteps_compress_base/1.1 steps. The three
# rungs are equally spaced (+0.015 each), so each ramp is ~1/3 of that:
#   33000/1.1/3 = 10000 steps per stage ramp.
variable nsteps_compress_base equal 33000
variable nsteps_compress      equal 30000    # 3× safety buffer PER STAGE ramp — halt fires ~10000
# nsteps: the length of EACH of the 3 per-stage equilibration/drain holds
# (NOT a single Phase-3 production length, and NOT the Stage 0 reference —
# that has its own nsteps_ref above). Passed from bash via -var nsteps.
# See NOTE at top of file: this has NOT yet been validated against a
# diffusion timescale.

# ----- Phase 0.5: Langevin + NPH barostat (replaces Nosé-Hoover NPT) -----
# Ported from slab_with_flow.lmp (compression_mode=1).  Nosé-Hoover NPT was
# replaced because FENE bonds inject kinetic energy faster than the NH chain
# can remove it (T runs away, bonds stretch toward R0=1.5 → "FENE bond too
# long").  A Langevin thermostat's per-atom friction removes energy in direct
# proportion to velocity and always wins against FENE heating; an NPH barostat
# sets the volume.
variable npt_P_damp equal 50.0   # NPH barostat damping (τ); raise to 500–1000 if FENE warnings persist
variable lang_T_damp equal 1.0   # Langevin damping (τ)
# NOTE: NPH targets the TOTAL pressure (incl. barostat virial).  We target
# P_target directly; if c_gel_press does not converge to ~${P_target}, add a
# small offset to the NPH target (slab_with_flow needed ≈ +0.41 for its system).

# Output frequencies
# index (not equal) style so a debug run can crank it up from the command line
# without editing the script:  lmp ... -var thermo_freq 1
# At the production value of 25000 there is a 25k-step blind spot between
# prints, which makes "hung" and "merely slow" look identical, and means the
# ONLY steps that appear are multiples of 25000 plus the first/last step of
# each run and each minimize.
variable thermo_freq     index 25000
variable dump_freq_setup equal 25000
variable dump_freq_prod  equal 25000
variable stress_freq     equal 10000

# fix halt check interval — DECOUPLED from stress_freq on purpose.
# fix halt only tests its condition every halt_freq steps, so the ramp always
# overshoots its target by up to one check interval. Overshoot in ε_vol is
# halt_freq * (target_strain_vol / ramp_steps_total) = halt_freq * 1.5e-6 at
# the current ramp speed (0.045 over ~30000 steps).
#   halt_freq = 500 -> 0.00075 overshoot = 5.0% of the 0.015 first rung
#   halt_freq = 100 -> 0.00015 overshoot = 1.0% of the 0.015 first rung
# 100 is used because the shortened ramps (10000 steps/stage, ~9.5x faster than
# the previous 285000-step reference) made 500 too coarse. Cost is evaluating
# the six plate-COM computes 5x more often during ramps only — negligible next
# to the holds.
variable halt_freq       equal 100

# Time averaging (stress) — adaptive
variable num_stress_curves equal 10
variable nevery_target     equal 100
variable nrepeat_max       equal 2000
variable nrepeat_min       equal 50

variable nfreq_raw    equal floor(${nsteps}/v_num_stress_curves)
variable nrepeat_raw  equal floor(v_nfreq_raw/v_nevery_target)

variable nr_lo equal (v_nrepeat_raw>v_nrepeat_min)*v_nrepeat_raw+(v_nrepeat_raw<=v_nrepeat_min)*v_nrepeat_min
variable nrepeat_stress equal (v_nr_lo<v_nrepeat_max)*v_nr_lo+(v_nr_lo>=v_nrepeat_max)*v_nrepeat_max
variable nevery_stress equal floor(v_nfreq_raw/v_nrepeat_stress)
variable nfreq_stress  equal v_nevery_stress*v_nrepeat_stress

print ">>> Stress averaging: nevery=${nevery_stress}  nrepeat=${nrepeat_stress}  nfreq=${nfreq_stress}"
print ">>> Compression (plate-driven, isotropic): ε_vol ladder = ${stage1_target} ${stage2_target} ${stage3_target}"
print ">>> Deepest ε_vol=${target_strain_vol} -> ε_axis=${target_strain_comp}  halt_freq=${halt_freq}  nsteps_compress=${nsteps_compress}"

# Spatial binning
variable binWidth    equal 2.0
variable rg_scale    equal 1.8
variable region_frac equal 1


# ==========================================================================
#                           INITIALIZATION
# ==========================================================================

units lj
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style molecular
atom_modify map array

# ── Domain decomposition / comm style ─────────────────────────────────────────
# balance_style selects BOTH the decomposition and the comm style — they are
# coupled: `balance rcb` REQUIRES comm_style tiled, `balance shift` REQUIRES the
# default regular grid (comm_style brick).  Set here (before read_data) so the
# very first decomposition already uses the chosen style.
#
#   shift (DEFAULT) — regular processor grid, movable cut planes per dimension.
#       Subdomains stay boxes on a regular lattice and ghost exchange stays on
#       the well-trodden brick code path.  Recovers most of the imbalance
#       because cuts move in all three dims (shift xyz).  Critically, `shift`
#       has a documented guard rcb does NOT: "if any pair of adjacent planes
#       are closer together than the neighbor skin distance ... the plane
#       positions are shifted to separate them by at least this amount ... to
#       prevent particles being lost when dynamics are run with processor
#       subdomains that are too narrow" (docs.lammps.org/balance.html).
#
#   rcb — recursive coordinate bisection (comm_style tiled).  Balances an
#       irregular density field better in principle, but on THIS geometry (a
#       dense gel block sitting in a sparse rho04 solvent box, 128 ranks over a
#       ~47.8 x 47.4 x 212 box) it carves the gel into thin tiles.  Once a tile
#       dimension approaches comm_modify cutoff (2.0 below) the tiled ghost
#       exchange degrades into multi-hop swaps and the run slows to a crawl or
#       stops making progress altogether.
#
#       This is the suspected cause of the 2026-07-24 stall (job 286541 on
#       node20): Phase 0 printed its step-25000 thermo line normally (T=0.998,
#       PE flat, dangerous builds 0 — no numerical problem), the next scheduled
#       `fix balance` rebalance was due at step 30000, and the job then produced
#       no output for ~2 h until it was cancelled.
#
#       Kept selectable so the two can be A/B'd:  lmp ... -var balance_style rcb
variable balance_style index shift

if "${balance_style} == rcb" then "comm_style tiled"

pair_style lj/cut 1.122
bond_style fene

read_data data_files/${dataname}.data nocoeff

# Ghost-atom communication cutoff. Must be >= the longest bond (FENE R0 = 1.5);
# 2.0 leaves margin. Previously 5.0, which made Nghost ~4x Nlocal and drove Comm
# to ~47% of wall time while Pair was only 0.14% (pair cutoff is just 1.122).
comm_modify cutoff 2.0

print "========================================"
print "Compression slab simulation (plate-driven): ${dataname}"
print "Interaction: epsSS=${epsSS}, epsSP=${epsSP}"
print "Production steps: ${nsteps}"
print "Target compressive strain (per axis): ${target_strain_comp}"
print "========================================"


# ==========================================================================
#                          GROUP DEFINITIONS
# ==========================================================================

group polymer    type 1 2
group backbone   type 1
group crosslinks type 2
group solvent    type 3
group gel        type 1 2 3      # all mobile gel atoms (NVT target)
group plate      type 4          # all plate atoms (all 6 plates combined)

# Individual plate subgroups (plate_top, plate_bot, etc.) are defined after
# Phase 1 equilibration in the GEL CHARACTERIZATION section below, once
# the plate mol IDs have been computed via compute reduce max mol.


# ==========================================================================
#                       INTERATOMIC POTENTIALS
# ==========================================================================

# WCA (purely repulsive) for all pairs by default
pair_coeff * * 1.0 ${sigma} 1.122

# Tunable polymer-solvent and solvent-solvent
pair_coeff 1 3 ${epsSP} ${sigma} 1.122
pair_coeff 2 3 ${epsSP} ${sigma} 1.122
pair_coeff 3 3 ${epsSS} ${sigma} 1.122

# Plate interactions:
#   Plate-plate interactions DISABLED — the six plates must not repel each
#   other across the gel (unlike shear_slab which only has two plates).
#   Plate-gel interactions: WCA (soft repulsive wall contact).
#   Plate-SOLVENT interactions DISABLED — plates must be transparent to solvent
#   so it flows through freely; measuring the NETWORK bulk modulus only.
#   (Previously WCA, which made plates push on the dense rho04 solvent layer at
#    the box faces → ~7.7e8 pressure → "Domain too large for neighbor bins".)
neigh_modify exclude type 4 4
neigh_modify exclude type 3 4
pair_coeff 4 4 0.0 ${sigma} 0.0               # plate-plate DISABLED
pair_coeff 1 4 1.0 ${sigma} 1.122             # polymer-plate WCA
pair_coeff 2 4 1.0 ${sigma} 1.122             # crosslinker-plate WCA
pair_coeff 3 4 0.0 ${sigma} 0.0               # solvent-plate DISABLED (solvent flows through)

# Type 5: orphan atoms left over from the pre-plate equilibration file (a
# single-axis "piston" support that add_more_plates_to_gel.py never strips
# out — it only deletes polymer near the boundary and passes every other
# atom type through unchanged). Not a real plate in this script's design.
# Without these lines it silently inherits the wildcard `pair_coeff * *`
# (full-strength WCA against solvent), which breaks the "plates transparent
# to solvent" design elsewhere. Mirror the type-4 treatment so it behaves
# the same way (frozen wall vs polymer, invisible to solvent) instead.
neigh_modify exclude type 4 5
neigh_modify exclude type 5 5
pair_coeff 5 5 0.0 ${sigma} 0.0               # orphan-orphan DISABLED
pair_coeff 4 5 0.0 ${sigma} 0.0               # orphan-plate DISABLED
pair_coeff 1 5 1.0 ${sigma} 1.122             # polymer-orphan WCA
pair_coeff 2 5 1.0 ${sigma} 1.122             # crosslinker-orphan WCA
pair_coeff 3 5 0.0 ${sigma} 0.0               # solvent-orphan DISABLED (transparent)

# Bond coefficients
bond_coeff 1 30.0 1.5 1.0 1.0   # polymer-polymer FENE (Kremer-Grest)

special_bonds fene
neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes

# ── Load balancing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-time repartition now (also speeds the upcoming minimize), then a periodic
# rebalance to track density changes through NPH (Phase 0.5) and compression
# (Phase 2).  Decomposition style is chosen by balance_style in the
# INITIALIZATION section above (default `shift`; `rcb` is the old behaviour).
#
# Cadence and threshold relaxed from the old (10000, 1.05):
#   - The box is FIXED through Phase 0 and Phase 1b, and across the ENTIRE
#     compression ladder the gel changes by only ε_vol = 0.045 (~1.5% per axis).
#     Density simply does not redistribute fast enough to justify a rebalance
#     every 10000 steps.
#   - A rebalance is not free: it forces a full atom migration plus neighbor-list
#     rebuild, and each one is another chance to land in a pathological
#     decomposition.  Fewer, looser rebalances is strictly safer here.
# Threshold 1.10 = rebalance only when the busiest rank exceeds the average by
# >10% (was 5%).
# index (not equal) style so both can be overridden from the command line
# alongside balance_style, e.g. -var balance_freq 20000
variable balance_freq   index 50000
variable balance_thresh index 1.10

# shift: `shift <dims> <Niter> <stopthresh>` — iteratively move the cut planes
# in x, y and z.  xyz (not just z) because the six-plate geometry makes the gel
# compact in all three directions, so the imbalance is not purely axial.
if "${balance_style} == rcb" then &
    "balance 1.0 rcb" &
    "fix balance all balance ${balance_freq} ${balance_thresh} rcb" &
else &
    "balance 1.0 shift xyz 20 1.05" &
    "fix balance all balance ${balance_freq} ${balance_thresh} shift xyz 10 1.05"

print ">>> Load balancing: style=${balance_style}  every ${balance_freq} steps  threshold=${balance_thresh}"


# ==========================================================================
#                           THERMO OUTPUT
# ==========================================================================

compute gel_temp  gel   temp
compute gel_press all   pressure gel_temp pair bond

# ── Global polymer osmotic stress (whole polymer / Rg gel volume) ──────────
# Defined here (before thermo_style) so σ_ii^poly and Π print from Phase 0
# onward — the gel volume V_gel(Rg) co-evolves with compression, which is
# exactly the Π-vs-V data the osmotic bulk modulus needs.
# See slab_with_flow.lmp for the stress/atom + Rg conventions reused below.
#
# compute stress/atom NULL → per-atom virial stress in pressure·volume units
#   (no kinetic term → configurational network stress only).  Summing the
#   diagonal over ALL polymer atoms and dividing by the gel volume converts
#   pressure·volume → pressure:        σ_ii^poly = Σ_a S_ii^a / V_gel.
# V_gel is the Rg-based gel volume (NOT the box volume).  For a uniform prism
#   L_i = 2√3·√(Rg_ii²)  and  V_gel = Lx_rg·Ly_rg·Lz_rg.  This is the same
#   Rg→length mapping used in slab_with_flow.lmp and later in this script.
compute rg_tensor       polymer gyration
compute stress_poly_all polymer stress/atom NULL
compute sumS_p_xx       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[1]
compute sumS_p_yy       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[2]
compute sumS_p_zz       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[3]
# Off-diagonal (shear) components of the same whole-polymer, Rg-normalised
# stress — added so σ_xy/σ_zx/σ_yz are available continuously (Phase 0->3)
# alongside the normal stresses, for the same time axis as Π and V_gel.
# stress/atom component order: [1]=xx [2]=yy [3]=zz [4]=xy [5]=xz [6]=yz.
compute sumS_p_xy       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[4]
compute sumS_p_zx       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[5]
compute sumS_p_yz       polymer reduce sum c_stress_poly_all[6]

variable gel_lx_rg  equal 2.0*sqrt(3.0*c_rg_tensor[1])
variable gel_ly_rg  equal 2.0*sqrt(3.0*c_rg_tensor[2])
variable gel_lz_rg  equal 2.0*sqrt(3.0*c_rg_tensor[3])
variable gel_vol_rg equal v_gel_lx_rg*v_gel_ly_rg*v_gel_lz_rg

# Polymer normal stresses normalised by the Rg gel volume → true pressure units.
variable sigP_xx equal c_sumS_p_xx/v_gel_vol_rg
variable sigP_yy equal c_sumS_p_yy/v_gel_vol_rg
variable sigP_zz equal c_sumS_p_zz/v_gel_vol_rg
# Off-diagonal counterparts (same normalisation).
variable sigP_xy equal c_sumS_p_xy/v_gel_vol_rg
variable sigP_zx equal c_sumS_p_zx/v_gel_vol_rg
variable sigP_yz equal c_sumS_p_yz/v_gel_vol_rg
# Total osmotic pressure = (1/3) tr(σ^poly).  (Sign follows the LAMMPS virial
# convention; take |Π| for a positive osmotic pressure — see plot script.)
variable Pi_osm  equal (v_sigP_xx+v_sigP_yy+v_sigP_zz)/3.0

# thermo_style: P_ij (pxx..pyz) removed; replaced by the polymer-only normal
# stresses and the total osmotic pressure Π so they are logged every thermo step.
thermo_style custom step c_gel_temp pe ke etotal press c_gel_press &
    v_sigP_xx v_sigP_yy v_sigP_zz v_Pi_osm vol lx ly lz xy xz yz
# ── Lost-atom handling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WAS: `lost warn`.  That setting is why the 2026-07-24 runs "died with no
# error": with `warn`, LAMMPS does NOT abort when atoms go missing — it prints a
# warning and keeps integrating a now-inconsistent system.  Whatever touches the
# missing atoms next (FENE bonds, the plate fixes, the stress/atom + reduce
# computes feeding sigP_*) then reads garbage or walks off an array, and the
# process dies silently instead of printing a diagnosable ERROR line.
#
# `error` restores the abort so LAMMPS names the actual failure.  Revert with
#   -var lost_atoms warn
# once the underlying problem is found (or if legitimately-escaping orphan
# type-5 atoms turn out to be the reason `warn` was set in the first place).
variable lost_atoms index error

# flush yes: force a flush after every thermo line.  Without it the tail of the
# output is lost in the stdio buffer when the process dies abnormally — so the
# last thing you see is NOT the last thing that happened.
thermo_modify lost ${lost_atoms} flush yes
thermo ${thermo_freq}


# ==========================================================================
#   PHASE 1: EQUILIBRATION  (Phase 0 NVT → Phase 0.5 Langevin+NPH → Phase 1b NVT)
# ==========================================================================
# Ported from slab_with_flow.lmp (compression_mode=1).  Replaces the previous
# Nosé-Hoover NPT (which let FENE bonds heat the system: "FENE bond too long").
#
# Phase 0   — NVT at fixed box volume, all plates frozen.  Settles the (cold)
#             starting config before any volume change.
# Phase 0.5 — Langevin thermostat + NPH iso barostat → P_target.  Plates are
#             released to nve+setforce so they scale isotropically with the box
#             (the old fix-move-0 pinned plates in absolute space while the box
#             shrank around them — a latent bug).  Re-frozen afterward.
# Phase 1b  — NVT at the new (NPH-final) box volume, plates re-frozen.  Relaxes
#             internal stresses at the correct density before compression.

print "========================================"
print "Phase 0: NVT equilibration (${nsteps_phase0} steps, fixed box, all plates frozen)"
print "========================================"

reset_timestep 0
timestep ${timestep_prod}

# Triclinic box required before any dump (LAMMPS restriction).
change_box all triclinic

dump traj_setup all custom ${dump_freq_setup} &
    traj_files/setup_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.lammpstrj &
    id type mol x y z

# Minimize with all plates frozen — only gel atoms relax around plates.
fix freeze_plates_min plate setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
velocity plate set 0.0 0.0 0.0
minimize 1.0e-4 1.0e-6 5000 50000
unfix freeze_plates_min

# Phase marker.  `minimize` advances the timestep counter by its ITERATION count,
# so the step number after this line is the number of CG iterations taken (11 in
# the 2026-07-24 run), not a dynamics step.  Because thermo_freq is 25000, a
# thermo line at a small step number like ~158 can ONLY have come from a minimize
# or from the first/last step of a run — this marker disambiguates which.
print ">>> Minimize COMPLETE: step=$(step) (= CG iterations)  T=$(c_gel_temp)  PE=$(pe)  Press=$(press)"

# Seed gel velocities at temp_target.  The input config is cold (T=0); without
# this the thermostats must heat from exactly zero, which is slow and leaves
# bonds pinned near R0.  (Addition beyond slab_with_flow, which starts from an
# already-equilibrated config that carries velocities.)
velocity gel create ${temp_target} 90210 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian

# ── OSMOTIC BULK-MODULUS DATA (Π, σ_ii^poly, gel volume) — all phases ──────
# Defined here (before Phase 0) and never unfixed, so it records continuously
# from Phase 0 through Phase 3.  Pairs the instantaneous polymer osmotic stress
# with the co-evolving Rg gel volume → the Π-vs-V_gel curve for the osmotic
# bulk modulus K = -V (dΠ/dV).  Post-processed in bulk_modulus_analysis.ipynb.
# Columns: step  σ_xx  σ_yy  σ_zz  σ_xy  σ_zx  σ_yz  Π  V_gel_rg  lx_rg  ly_rg  lz_rg
# (off-diagonal columns added so bulk_modulus_analysis.ipynb can plot the
#  shear stresses on the same continuous time axis as everything else; older
#  9-column data files from before this change remain readable — the notebook
#  reader detects the column count.)
fix out_bulk_modulus all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) $(v_sigP_xx) $(v_sigP_yy) $(v_sigP_zz) $(v_sigP_xy) $(v_sigP_zx) $(v_sigP_yz) $(v_Pi_osm) $(v_gel_vol_rg) $(v_gel_lx_rg) $(v_gel_ly_rg) $(v_gel_lz_rg)" &
    title "# step sigP_xx sigP_yy sigP_zz sigP_xy sigP_zx sigP_yz Pi_osm V_gel_rg lx_rg ly_rg lz_rg" &
    file output_files/stress_data/bulk_modulus_plot_data_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no

# --- Phase 0: Langevin+NVE at fixed box volume ---
# Was plain Nosé-Hoover `fix nvt`. Swapped for the same reason Phase 0.5's
# barostat thermostat was swapped (see note above Phase 0.5): FENE bonds can
# inject kinetic energy faster than an NH chain can remove it, and this phase
# immediately follows `velocity gel create` dumping a fresh Gaussian velocity
# distribution onto a previously cold, minimized, dense (rho04) system —
# exactly the situation where NH falls behind. Langevin's per-atom friction
# does not have that lag. Box is still fixed here (no barostat), so nothing
# else about Phase 0 changes.
fix freeze_plates_0 plate   move linear 0 0 0
fix nve_phase0      gel     nve
fix lang_phase0     gel     langevin ${temp_target} ${temp_target} ${lang_T_damp} 90211
fix mom_phase0      gel     momentum 100 linear 1 1 1

run ${nsteps_phase0}

unfix mom_phase0
unfix lang_phase0
unfix nve_phase0
unfix freeze_plates_0

print ">>> Post-Phase-0 NVT  T = $(c_gel_temp)  P = $(press)  c_gel_press = $(c_gel_press)"

# --- Phase 0.5: Langevin + NPH iso to P_target (plates scale with box) ---
print "========================================"
print "Phase 0.5: Langevin+NPH iso to P = ${P_target} (${nsteps_npt} steps, plates scale with box)"
print "========================================"

# Release plates: nve + setforce 0 → zero net force, integrated, and remapped
# by the NPH barostat (dilate all) so they scale isotropically with the box.
velocity plate set 0.0 0.0 0.0
fix nve_plate      plate nve
fix setforce_plate plate setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0

# Langevin (per-atom friction beats FENE heating) + NPH barostat.
fix lang_p05 gel langevin ${temp_target} ${temp_target} ${lang_T_damp} 48279
fix nph_p05  gel nph iso ${P_target} ${P_target} ${npt_P_damp}

run ${nsteps_npt}

unfix nph_p05
unfix lang_p05

print ">>> Post-Langevin+NPH  T = $(c_gel_temp)  c_gel_press = $(c_gel_press)  box = $(lx) x $(ly) x $(lz)"

# Re-freeze plates at their new (scaled) positions.
unfix nve_plate
unfix setforce_plate
velocity plate set 0.0 0.0 0.0

# --- Phase 1b: NVT at the NPH-final volume ---
print "========================================"
print "Phase 1b: NVT equilibration (${nsteps_equil} steps, plates frozen at NPH volume)"
print "========================================"

fix freeze_plates_1 plate   move linear 0 0 0
fix nvt_equil       gel     nvt temp ${temp_target} ${temp_target} 1.0
fix mom_equil       gel     momentum 100 linear 1 1 1

run ${nsteps_equil}

unfix mom_equil
unfix nvt_equil
unfix freeze_plates_1

print ">>> Post-NVT T = $(c_gel_temp)  P = $(press)  c_gel_press = $(c_gel_press)"
print ">>> Box after Phase 1: $(lx) x $(ly) x $(lz)"


# ==========================================================================
#          GEL CHARACTERIZATION & PLATE SETUP (post-equilibration)
# ==========================================================================
# Identify individual plates by mol ID. add_more_plates_to_gel.ipynb assigns
# mol IDs max_mol_gel+1..+6 (top, bot, front, back, right, left in order).
# We compute the max mol ID of gel atoms (types 1 2 3) at this point.
#
# Note: spatial region grouping cannot be used here because the right/left
# plates span the full box y-range, which overlaps the y-positions of the
# front/back plates. Mol ID is the only unambiguous identifier.

compute polymer_com  polymer com
compute minx_polymer polymer reduce min x
compute maxx_polymer polymer reduce max x
compute miny_polymer polymer reduce min y
compute maxy_polymer polymer reduce max y
compute minz_polymer polymer reduce min z
compute maxz_polymer polymer reduce max z
# compute rg_tensor and the gel_lx/ly/lz/vol_rg variables are now defined
# earlier (THERMO OUTPUT section) so they are available from Phase 0; the
# duplicate definitions that lived here have been removed.

# Atom-style variable used to access mol ID per atom in compute reduce
variable mol_id atom mol
compute max_mol_gel gel reduce max v_mol_id

run 0

variable gel_xlo equal $(c_minx_polymer)
variable gel_xhi equal $(c_maxx_polymer)
variable gel_ylo equal $(c_miny_polymer)
variable gel_yhi equal $(c_maxy_polymer)
variable gel_zlo equal $(c_minz_polymer)
variable gel_zhi equal $(c_maxz_polymer)

print ">>> Gel x-extent: ${gel_xlo} to ${gel_xhi}  (lx_gel = $(v_gel_xhi - v_gel_xlo) σ)"
print ">>> Gel y-extent: ${gel_ylo} to ${gel_yhi}  (ly_gel = $(v_gel_yhi - v_gel_ylo) σ)"
print ">>> Gel z-extent: ${gel_zlo} to ${gel_zhi}  (lz_gel = $(v_gel_zhi - v_gel_zlo) σ)"
print ">>> Gel Rg dims: $(v_gel_lx_rg) x $(v_gel_ly_rg) x $(v_gel_lz_rg)"

# Rg half-widths (for bulk region sizing — frozen as constants after Phase 2)
variable eps   equal 1.0e-12
variable Rg_xx equal c_rg_tensor[1]
variable Rg_yy equal c_rg_tensor[2]
variable Rg_zz equal c_rg_tensor[3]
variable hw_x equal v_region_frac*v_rg_scale*sqrt(v_Rg_xx + v_eps)
variable hw_y equal v_region_frac*v_rg_scale*sqrt(v_Rg_yy + v_eps)
variable hw_z equal v_region_frac*v_rg_scale*sqrt(v_Rg_zz + v_eps)

# ── Assign individual plate groups by mol ID ──────────────────────────────────
variable mol_top_plate   equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+1)
variable mol_bot_plate   equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+2)
variable mol_front_plate equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+3)
variable mol_back_plate  equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+4)
variable mol_right_plate equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+5)
variable mol_left_plate  equal round($(c_max_mol_gel)+6)

print ">>> Plate mol IDs: top=${mol_top_plate}  bot=${mol_bot_plate}  front=${mol_front_plate}  back=${mol_back_plate}  right=${mol_right_plate}  left=${mol_left_plate}"

# Use the group command's native 'molecule' style (works on all LAMMPS
# versions). The earlier atom-style-variable approach used the 'mol' keyword,
# which is only a valid atom-style vector in newer LAMMPS builds and fails with
# "Invalid syntax in variable formula" on older cluster builds.
group plate_top   molecule ${mol_top_plate}
group plate_bot   molecule ${mol_bot_plate}
group plate_front molecule ${mol_front_plate}
group plate_back  molecule ${mol_back_plate}
group plate_right molecule ${mol_right_plate}
group plate_left  molecule ${mol_left_plate}

print ">>> plate_top: $(count(plate_top))  plate_bot: $(count(plate_bot))"
print ">>> plate_front: $(count(plate_front))  plate_back: $(count(plate_back))"
print ">>> plate_right: $(count(plate_right))  plate_left: $(count(plate_left))"

# ── Plate COM computes (for strain tracking and velocity scaling) ─────────────
compute com_top   plate_top   com
compute com_bot   plate_bot   com
compute com_front plate_front com
compute com_back  plate_back  com
compute com_right plate_right com
compute com_left  plate_left  com

# ── Plate force computes (net force from the gel on each plate) ────────────────
# reduce sum f{x,y,z} over each plate's atoms = the net pair+bond force LAMMPS
# computed on those atoms this step. Plates are held with `fix move linear`
# (kinematic — sets x/v directly, does NOT zero the per-atom force array), so
# this is the genuine reaction force the gel exerts on the plate, during Phase
# 1b, Phase 2 (driven), and Phase 3 (frozen post-compression).
# EXCEPTION: during Phase 0.5 (Langevin+NPH) the plates run under
# `fix setforce 0 0 0`, which DOES zero the force array — expect exactly 0
# there; that is correct, not a bug.
# SCOPE: individual plate identity (top vs bot vs ...) only exists once the
# mol-ID resolution above has run, i.e. after Phase 0/0.5/1b equilibration —
# so this is the earliest point these six plates can be tracked separately;
# it is not available from step 0 of Phase 0.
compute f_top_x   plate_top   reduce sum fx
compute f_top_y   plate_top   reduce sum fy
compute f_top_z   plate_top   reduce sum fz
compute f_bot_x   plate_bot   reduce sum fx
compute f_bot_y   plate_bot   reduce sum fy
compute f_bot_z   plate_bot   reduce sum fz
compute f_front_x plate_front reduce sum fx
compute f_front_y plate_front reduce sum fy
compute f_front_z plate_front reduce sum fz
compute f_back_x  plate_back  reduce sum fx
compute f_back_y  plate_back  reduce sum fy
compute f_back_z  plate_back  reduce sum fz
compute f_right_x plate_right reduce sum fx
compute f_right_y plate_right reduce sum fy
compute f_right_z plate_right reduce sum fz
compute f_left_x  plate_left  reduce sum fx
compute f_left_y  plate_left  reduce sum fy
compute f_left_z  plate_left  reduce sum fz

# Columns: step  {top,bot,front,back,right,left}_{fx,fy,fz}  (18 force values)
fix out_plate_force all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) $(c_f_top_x) $(c_f_top_y) $(c_f_top_z) $(c_f_bot_x) $(c_f_bot_y) $(c_f_bot_z) $(c_f_front_x) $(c_f_front_y) $(c_f_front_z) $(c_f_back_x) $(c_f_back_y) $(c_f_back_z) $(c_f_right_x) $(c_f_right_y) $(c_f_right_z) $(c_f_left_x) $(c_f_left_y) $(c_f_left_z)" &
    title "# step top_fx top_fy top_fz bot_fx bot_fy bot_fz front_fx front_fy front_fz back_fx back_fy back_fz right_fx right_fy right_fz left_fx left_fy left_fz" &
    file output_files/stress_data/plate_force_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no

run 0

# Initial plate-to-plate gaps (frozen as reference values)
variable gap_z_0 equal $(c_com_top[3]   - c_com_bot[3])
variable gap_y_0 equal $(c_com_front[2] - c_com_back[2])
variable gap_x_0 equal $(c_com_right[1] - c_com_left[1])

print ">>> Plate-to-plate gaps (initial): x = ${gap_x_0}  y = ${gap_y_0}  z = ${gap_z_0}"

# Live gap variables (evaluated each time they appear in output/halt)
variable gap_z_current equal (c_com_top[3]   - c_com_bot[3])
variable gap_y_current equal (c_com_front[2] - c_com_back[2])
variable gap_x_current equal (c_com_right[1] - c_com_left[1])

# Compressive strain per axis: positive = compression
variable compress_strain_z   equal (v_gap_z_0 - v_gap_z_current) / v_gap_z_0
variable compress_strain_y   equal (v_gap_y_0 - v_gap_y_current) / v_gap_y_0
variable compress_strain_x   equal (v_gap_x_0 - v_gap_x_current) / v_gap_x_0
variable compress_strain_vol equal 1.0 - (1.0-v_compress_strain_x)*(1.0-v_compress_strain_y)*(1.0-v_compress_strain_z)

# Plate velocities: 1.1× the speed that reaches target_strain in nsteps_compress_base steps.
# Each plate moves inward by (target_strain * gap_0 / 2) over nsteps_compress_base steps.
# The run is halted by fix halt, so nsteps_compress is just a 3× safety buffer
# (30000 cap vs ~10000 actual per stage ramp).
variable vcompress_z equal $(v_target_strain_comp * v_gap_z_0 / (2.0 * v_nsteps_compress_base * v_timestep_prod) * 1.1)
variable vcompress_y equal $(v_target_strain_comp * v_gap_y_0 / (2.0 * v_nsteps_compress_base * v_timestep_prod) * 1.1)
variable vcompress_x equal $(v_target_strain_comp * v_gap_x_0 / (2.0 * v_nsteps_compress_base * v_timestep_prod) * 1.1)

print ">>> vcompress_z = ${vcompress_z}  vcompress_y = ${vcompress_y}  vcompress_x = ${vcompress_x}"
print ">>> (1.1× base speed; halt fires on compress_strain_vol, checked every ${halt_freq} steps)"


# ==========================================================================
#             BULK REGION (exclude 3σ near each plate face)
# ==========================================================================
# Atoms within 3σ of any plate face carry artifactual constraint stresses
# from the harmonic plate-polymer bonds. Exclude all six faces.
#
# Defined ONCE here, using the PRE-compression gel geometry (gel_xlo/xhi/...
# from the GEL CHARACTERIZATION section above) — see NOTE at top of file.
# The same physical atoms (poly_bulk/solv_bulk) are tracked through all 5
# compression stages below, rather than re-snapshotted per stage.

variable xlo_bulk equal ${gel_xlo}+3.0
variable xhi_bulk equal ${gel_xhi}-3.0
variable ylo_bulk equal ${gel_ylo}+3.0
variable yhi_bulk equal ${gel_yhi}-3.0
variable zlo_bulk equal ${gel_zlo}+3.0
variable zhi_bulk equal ${gel_zhi}-3.0
variable bulk_lx  equal v_xhi_bulk-v_xlo_bulk
variable bulk_ly  equal v_yhi_bulk-v_ylo_bulk
variable bulk_lz  equal v_zhi_bulk-v_zlo_bulk
variable bulk_vol equal v_bulk_lx*v_bulk_ly*v_bulk_lz

region reg_bulk block ${xlo_bulk} ${xhi_bulk} ${ylo_bulk} ${yhi_bulk} ${zlo_bulk} ${zhi_bulk} units box
group all_bulk  region reg_bulk
group poly_bulk intersect polymer all_bulk
group solv_bulk intersect solvent all_bulk

print ">>> Bulk x: ${xlo_bulk} to ${xhi_bulk}  (lx = $(v_bulk_lx))"
print ">>> Bulk y: ${ylo_bulk} to ${yhi_bulk}  (ly = $(v_bulk_ly))"
print ">>> Bulk z: ${zlo_bulk} to ${zhi_bulk}  (lz = $(v_bulk_lz))"
print ">>> bulk_vol = $(v_bulk_vol)"
print ">>> poly_bulk: $(count(poly_bulk))  solv_bulk: $(count(solv_bulk))"


# ==========================================================================
#                    ANALYSIS: PARTIAL STRESSES
# ==========================================================================

compute stress_polymer poly_bulk stress/atom NULL
compute stress_solvent solv_bulk stress/atom NULL

# Box-integrated polymer stress (bulk only)
compute sig_p_xx poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[1]
compute sig_p_yy poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[2]
compute sig_p_zz poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[3]
compute sig_p_xy poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[4]
compute sig_p_zx poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[5]
compute sig_p_yz poly_bulk reduce sum c_stress_polymer[6]

variable stress_p_xx equal c_sig_p_xx/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_p_yy equal c_sig_p_yy/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_p_zz equal c_sig_p_zz/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_p_xy equal c_sig_p_xy/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_p_zx equal c_sig_p_zx/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_p_yz equal c_sig_p_yz/v_bulk_vol

# Box-integrated solvent stress (bulk only)
compute sig_s_xx solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[1]
compute sig_s_yy solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[2]
compute sig_s_zz solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[3]
compute sig_s_xy solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[4]
compute sig_s_zx solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[5]
compute sig_s_yz solv_bulk reduce sum c_stress_solvent[6]

variable stress_s_xx equal c_sig_s_xx/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_s_yy equal c_sig_s_yy/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_s_zz equal c_sig_s_zz/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_s_xy equal c_sig_s_xy/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_s_zx equal c_sig_s_zx/v_bulk_vol
variable stress_s_yz equal c_sig_s_yz/v_bulk_vol

# Per-atom z-bin stress (slabs normal to z — the top/bot compression axis)
# Bin volume = binWidth * Lx * Ly
variable s_p_xx atom c_stress_polymer[1]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_p_yy atom c_stress_polymer[2]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_p_zz atom c_stress_polymer[3]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_p_xy atom c_stress_polymer[4]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_p_zx atom c_stress_polymer[5]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_p_yz atom c_stress_polymer[6]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)

variable s_s_xx atom c_stress_solvent[1]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_s_yy atom c_stress_solvent[2]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_s_zz atom c_stress_solvent[3]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_s_xy atom c_stress_solvent[4]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_s_zx atom c_stress_solvent[5]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)
variable s_s_yz atom c_stress_solvent[6]/(${binWidth}*lx*ly)


# ==========================================================================
#                    ANALYSIS: SPATIAL CHUNKS (z-binning)
# ==========================================================================
# Bin along z (top/bot compression direction; also the long axis of the gel)

variable binWidth_reduced equal $(v_binWidth/lz)
compute chunk_z_polymer poly_bulk chunk/atom bin/1d z lower ${binWidth_reduced} units reduced
compute chunk_z_solvent  solv_bulk chunk/atom bin/1d z lower ${binWidth_reduced} units reduced


# ==========================================================================
#    OUTPUT: GEL AND BOX DIMENSIONS (continuous through all 3 stages)
# ==========================================================================

fix out_gel_dims_rg all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) $(v_gel_lx_rg) $(v_gel_ly_rg) $(v_gel_lz_rg)" &
    file output_files/volume_data/gel_dimensions_rg_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no

fix out_box_dims all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) $(lx) $(ly) $(lz) $(xy) $(xz) $(yz)" &
    file output_files/volume_data/box_dimensions_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no

fix out_polymer_com all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) $(c_polymer_com[1]) $(c_polymer_com[2]) $(c_polymer_com[3])" &
    file output_files/volume_data/polymer_com_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no


# ==========================================================================
#      PHASE 2/3 STAGED: COMPRESS -> FREEZE -> DRAIN/EQUILIBRATE -> MEASURE
# ==========================================================================
# 3 stages, cumulative compress_strain_vol targets = stage1..stage3_target.
# Each stage: (a) drive plates to that stage's target strain (Langevin+NVE,
# same as the old single-shot Phase 2), (b) freeze all 6 plates and hold NVT
# for `nsteps` steps so the solvent can redistribute/drain, (c) average the
# equilibrated stress tensor over that hold. stress_tensor_polymer/solvent
# and stress_profile_z_* accumulate ALL 3 stages into the same file (stage 1
# creates it, stages 2-3 append) — only equilibrated-hold data goes in, ramp
# periods are skipped. compress_strain_*.dat and the dims/COM files above are
# never unfixed, so they run continuously across ramps AND holds for all 3
# stages in one file each (this is what shows the staircase downstream).
#
# Sign convention (each plate moves toward gel center):
#   Top   (+z face): vz = -vcompress_z   Bot   (-z face): vz = +vcompress_z
#   Front (+y face): vy = -vcompress_y   Back  (-y face): vy = +vcompress_y
#   Right (+x face): vx = -vcompress_x   Left  (-x face): vx = +vcompress_x

undump traj_setup
dump traj_prod all custom ${dump_freq_prod} &
    traj_files/prod_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.lammpstrj &
    id type mol x y z

# Output: step  gap_z_0  gap_z_current  compress_strain_z  compress_strain_vol
# Defined once, never unfixed — covers ramps + holds for all 3 stages.
fix out_compress_strain all print ${stress_freq} &
    "$(step) ${gap_z_0} $(v_gap_z_current) $(v_compress_strain_z) $(v_compress_strain_vol)" &
    file output_files/stress_data/compress_strain_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat screen no


# ==========================================================================
#          STAGE 0: ε_vol = 0 REFERENCE (undeformed baseline)
# ==========================================================================
# Ported from slab_with_flow.lmp's ref_ fix block. Records the bulk-region
# polymer and solvent stresses at ZERO strain, over the same poly_bulk/
# solv_bulk groups, the same bulk_vol normalisation and the same averaging
# window (nevery/nrepeat/nfreq) as the 3 stage holds — so P'_net(ε_vol=0) is
# measured, not assumed. Its LENGTH is nsteps_ref, set independently of the
# stage-hold length so the baseline can be averaged for as long as it needs
# without lengthening every stage.
#
# WHY: bulk_modulus_analysis.ipynb's K_single = P'_net(ε)/ε carries an
# "implicit zero at the pre-compression state". For a swollen, pre-stressed
# network the at-rest Terzaghi effective stress is NOT generally zero, so that
# assumption biases K_single by an unknown amount. The 3-point linear fit is
# reference-independent and doesn't need this, but with the tighter ε_vol
# ladder the signals are small enough that an anchored zero is worth having —
# it also gives the fit a 4th point at the origin and lets you check the
# fitted intercept against a measured value.
#
# Plates are frozen and the gel is on NVT — identical dynamics to a stage
# hold, just with no preceding ramp. Uses `file` (not `append`) so the ref
# lands in its own *_ref_*.dat, leaving the 3-stage files untouched.
#
# Only fix ave/time here (no ave/chunk), so no compute chunk/atom lock is
# taken; the run is still epoch-aligned so the final averaging window
# actually completes and writes its row.

print "========================================"
print "Stage 0/3: ε_vol = 0 reference (undeformed baseline, ${nsteps_ref} steps)"
print "========================================"

fix freeze_top   plate_top   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_bot   plate_bot   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_front plate_front move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_back  plate_back  move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_right plate_right move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_left  plate_left  move linear 0 0 0
fix nvt_ref      gel         nvt  temp ${temp_target} ${temp_target} 1.0
fix mom_ref      gel         momentum 100 linear 1 1 1 angular

fix ref_avg_stress_polymer all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_p_xx v_stress_p_yy v_stress_p_zz &
    v_stress_p_xy v_stress_p_zx v_stress_p_yz &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_polymer_ref_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix ref_avg_stress_solvent all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_s_xx v_stress_s_yy v_stress_s_zz &
    v_stress_s_xy v_stress_s_zx v_stress_s_yz &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_solvent_ref_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

# Epoch-aligned (same formula as the stage holds — see NOTE at top of file).
# Uses nsteps_ref, NOT nsteps: the reference hold has its own length. The
# averaging window (nevery/nrepeat/nfreq_stress) is still the stage window, so
# the ref rows are directly comparable to the stage rows — nsteps_ref just
# controls how many such rows the baseline gets.
variable hold_steps equal (floor(($(step)+${nsteps_ref}-1)/${nfreq_stress})+1)*${nfreq_stress}-$(step)
print ">>> Stage 0 (ref) aligned: ${hold_steps} steps (requested ${nsteps_ref}, nfreq_stress=${nfreq_stress})"

run ${hold_steps}

unfix ref_avg_stress_solvent
unfix ref_avg_stress_polymer
unfix mom_ref
unfix nvt_ref
unfix freeze_left
unfix freeze_right
unfix freeze_back
unfix freeze_front
unfix freeze_bot
unfix freeze_top

print ">>> Stage 0 (ref) done: compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol) (should be ~0) stress_p_zz=$(v_stress_p_zz) stress_s_zz=$(v_stress_s_zz)"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stage 1 --
print "========================================"
print "Stage 1/3: compress to compress_strain_vol = ${stage1_target}  (ε_axis ~ 0.005)"
print "========================================"

fix drive_top   plate_top   move linear  0             0            -${vcompress_z}
fix drive_bot   plate_bot   move linear  0             0             ${vcompress_z}
fix drive_front plate_front move linear  0            -${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_back  plate_back  move linear  0             ${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_right plate_right move linear -${vcompress_x}  0           0
fix drive_left  plate_left  move linear  ${vcompress_x}  0           0

fix nve_compress  gel     nve
fix lang_compress gel     langevin ${temp_target} ${temp_target} ${lang_T_damp} 71623
fix mom_lin_c     gel     momentum 100 linear 1 1 1
fix mom_rot_c     gel     momentum 100 angular

fix halt_compress all halt ${halt_freq} v_compress_strain_vol >= ${stage1_target} error continue

run ${nsteps_compress}

unfix halt_compress
unfix mom_rot_c
unfix mom_lin_c
unfix lang_compress
unfix nve_compress
unfix drive_left
unfix drive_right
unfix drive_back
unfix drive_front
unfix drive_bot
unfix drive_top

print ">>> Stage 1 compression done: compress_strain_z=$(v_compress_strain_z) compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol)"
print "Stage 1/3: freeze + NVT drain/equilibrate (${nsteps} steps)"

fix freeze_top   plate_top   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_bot   plate_bot   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_front plate_front move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_back  plate_back  move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_right plate_right move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_left  plate_left  move linear 0 0 0
fix nvt_prod     gel         nvt  temp ${temp_target} ${temp_target} 1.0
fix mom_prod     gel         momentum 100 linear 1 1 1 angular

fix avg_stress_polymer all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_p_xx v_stress_p_yy v_stress_p_zz &
    v_stress_p_xy v_stress_p_zx v_stress_p_yz &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix avg_stress_solvent all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_s_xx v_stress_s_yy v_stress_s_zz &
    v_stress_s_xy v_stress_s_zx v_stress_s_yz &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_polymer poly_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_polymer &
    v_s_p_xx v_s_p_yy v_s_p_zz v_s_p_xy v_s_p_zx v_s_p_yz &
    norm none &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_solvent solv_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_solvent &
    v_s_s_xx v_s_s_yy v_s_s_zz v_s_s_xy v_s_s_zx v_s_s_yz &
    norm none &
    file output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

# ── Epoch-aligned hold length (see NOTE on epoch alignment at top of file) ────
# Pads the hold to the first multiple of nfreq_stress at or beyond
# step+nsteps, so fix ave/chunk finishes its last epoch and releases the
# compute chunk/atom lock before the unfix below. Always >= nsteps.
# $(step) is expanded immediately, so this line MUST be repeated at each
# stage rather than hoisted (equal-style variables are redefinable, so
# reusing the name across stages is fine).
variable hold_steps equal (floor(($(step)+${nsteps}-1)/${nfreq_stress})+1)*${nfreq_stress}-$(step)
print ">>> Stage 1 hold aligned: ${hold_steps} steps (requested ${nsteps}, nfreq_stress=${nfreq_stress})"

run ${hold_steps}

unfix prof_z_solvent
unfix prof_z_polymer
unfix avg_stress_solvent
unfix avg_stress_polymer
unfix mom_prod
unfix nvt_prod
unfix freeze_left
unfix freeze_right
unfix freeze_back
unfix freeze_front
unfix freeze_bot
unfix freeze_top

print ">>> Stage 1 hold done: compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol) stress_p_zz=$(v_stress_p_zz) stress_s_zz=$(v_stress_s_zz)"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stage 2 --
print "========================================"
print "Stage 2/3: compress to compress_strain_vol = ${stage2_target}  (ε_axis ~ 0.0101)"
print "========================================"

fix drive_top   plate_top   move linear  0             0            -${vcompress_z}
fix drive_bot   plate_bot   move linear  0             0             ${vcompress_z}
fix drive_front plate_front move linear  0            -${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_back  plate_back  move linear  0             ${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_right plate_right move linear -${vcompress_x}  0           0
fix drive_left  plate_left  move linear  ${vcompress_x}  0           0

fix nve_compress  gel     nve
fix lang_compress gel     langevin ${temp_target} ${temp_target} ${lang_T_damp} 71623
fix mom_lin_c     gel     momentum 100 linear 1 1 1
fix mom_rot_c     gel     momentum 100 angular

fix halt_compress all halt ${halt_freq} v_compress_strain_vol >= ${stage2_target} error continue

run ${nsteps_compress}

unfix halt_compress
unfix mom_rot_c
unfix mom_lin_c
unfix lang_compress
unfix nve_compress
unfix drive_left
unfix drive_right
unfix drive_back
unfix drive_front
unfix drive_bot
unfix drive_top

print ">>> Stage 2 compression done: compress_strain_z=$(v_compress_strain_z) compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol)"
print "Stage 2/3: freeze + NVT drain/equilibrate (${nsteps} steps)"

fix freeze_top   plate_top   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_bot   plate_bot   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_front plate_front move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_back  plate_back  move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_right plate_right move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_left  plate_left  move linear 0 0 0
fix nvt_prod     gel         nvt  temp ${temp_target} ${temp_target} 1.0
fix mom_prod     gel         momentum 100 linear 1 1 1 angular

fix avg_stress_polymer all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_p_xx v_stress_p_yy v_stress_p_zz &
    v_stress_p_xy v_stress_p_zx v_stress_p_yz &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix avg_stress_solvent all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_s_xx v_stress_s_yy v_stress_s_zz &
    v_stress_s_xy v_stress_s_zx v_stress_s_yz &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_polymer poly_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_polymer &
    v_s_p_xx v_s_p_yy v_s_p_zz v_s_p_xy v_s_p_zx v_s_p_yz &
    norm none &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_solvent solv_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_solvent &
    v_s_s_xx v_s_s_yy v_s_s_zz v_s_s_xy v_s_s_zx v_s_s_yz &
    norm none &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

# Epoch-aligned hold length — see Stage 1 and the NOTE at top of file.
variable hold_steps equal (floor(($(step)+${nsteps}-1)/${nfreq_stress})+1)*${nfreq_stress}-$(step)
print ">>> Stage 2 hold aligned: ${hold_steps} steps (requested ${nsteps}, nfreq_stress=${nfreq_stress})"

run ${hold_steps}

unfix prof_z_solvent
unfix prof_z_polymer
unfix avg_stress_solvent
unfix avg_stress_polymer
unfix mom_prod
unfix nvt_prod
unfix freeze_left
unfix freeze_right
unfix freeze_back
unfix freeze_front
unfix freeze_bot
unfix freeze_top

print ">>> Stage 2 hold done: compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol) stress_p_zz=$(v_stress_p_zz) stress_s_zz=$(v_stress_s_zz)"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stage 3 --
print "========================================"
print "Stage 3/3: compress to compress_strain_vol = ${stage3_target}  (ε_axis ~ 0.0152)"
print "========================================"

fix drive_top   plate_top   move linear  0             0            -${vcompress_z}
fix drive_bot   plate_bot   move linear  0             0             ${vcompress_z}
fix drive_front plate_front move linear  0            -${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_back  plate_back  move linear  0             ${vcompress_y}  0
fix drive_right plate_right move linear -${vcompress_x}  0           0
fix drive_left  plate_left  move linear  ${vcompress_x}  0           0

fix nve_compress  gel     nve
fix lang_compress gel     langevin ${temp_target} ${temp_target} ${lang_T_damp} 71623
fix mom_lin_c     gel     momentum 100 linear 1 1 1
fix mom_rot_c     gel     momentum 100 angular

fix halt_compress all halt ${halt_freq} v_compress_strain_vol >= ${stage3_target} error continue

run ${nsteps_compress}

unfix halt_compress
unfix mom_rot_c
unfix mom_lin_c
unfix lang_compress
unfix nve_compress
unfix drive_left
unfix drive_right
unfix drive_back
unfix drive_front
unfix drive_bot
unfix drive_top

print ">>> Stage 3 compression done: compress_strain_z=$(v_compress_strain_z) compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol)"
print "Stage 3/3: freeze + NVT drain/equilibrate (${nsteps} steps)"

fix freeze_top   plate_top   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_bot   plate_bot   move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_front plate_front move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_back  plate_back  move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_right plate_right move linear 0 0 0
fix freeze_left  plate_left  move linear 0 0 0
fix nvt_prod     gel         nvt  temp ${temp_target} ${temp_target} 1.0
fix mom_prod     gel         momentum 100 linear 1 1 1 angular

fix avg_stress_polymer all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_p_xx v_stress_p_yy v_stress_p_zz &
    v_stress_p_xy v_stress_p_zx v_stress_p_yz &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix avg_stress_solvent all ave/time ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    v_stress_s_xx v_stress_s_yy v_stress_s_zz &
    v_stress_s_xy v_stress_s_zx v_stress_s_yz &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_tensor_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_polymer poly_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_polymer &
    v_s_p_xx v_s_p_yy v_s_p_zz v_s_p_xy v_s_p_zx v_s_p_yz &
    norm none &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_polymer_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

fix prof_z_solvent solv_bulk ave/chunk ${nevery_stress} ${nrepeat_stress} ${nfreq_stress} &
    chunk_z_solvent &
    v_s_s_xx v_s_s_yy v_s_s_zz v_s_s_xy v_s_s_zx v_s_s_yz &
    norm none &
    append output_files/stress_data/stress_profile_z_solvent_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}.dat

# Epoch-aligned hold length — see Stage 1 and the NOTE at top of file.
# Still required on this (final) stage: the ave/chunk fixes are unfixed below,
# and leaving a dangling lock would poison any continuation run.
variable hold_steps equal (floor(($(step)+${nsteps}-1)/${nfreq_stress})+1)*${nfreq_stress}-$(step)
print ">>> Stage 3 hold aligned: ${hold_steps} steps (requested ${nsteps}, nfreq_stress=${nfreq_stress})"

run ${hold_steps}

unfix prof_z_solvent
unfix prof_z_polymer
unfix avg_stress_solvent
unfix avg_stress_polymer

print ">>> Stage 3 hold done: compress_strain_vol=$(v_compress_strain_vol) stress_p_zz=$(v_stress_p_zz) stress_s_zz=$(v_stress_s_zz)"


# ==========================================================================
#                            CLEANUP
# ==========================================================================
# Plates are left frozen at their Stage-3 (final) positions, matching the
# original single-shot script's end state. The freeze/nvt/mom fixes from the
# Stage 3 hold are still active here — that is why they are torn down below
# rather than at the end of the stage block.

undump traj_prod
unfix mom_prod
unfix nvt_prod
unfix freeze_left
unfix freeze_right
unfix freeze_back
unfix freeze_front
unfix freeze_bot
unfix freeze_top

print "========================================"
print "Compression slab simulation complete (3-stage slope method)"
print "  compress_strain_z   = $(v_compress_strain_z)"
print "  compress_strain_y   = $(v_compress_strain_y)"
print "  compress_strain_x   = $(v_compress_strain_x)"
print "  compress_strain_vol = $(v_compress_strain_vol)  (= final ε_vol)"
print "  gel (Rg): $(v_gel_lx_rg) x $(v_gel_ly_rg) x $(v_gel_lz_rg)"
print "  Final box: $(lx) x $(ly) x $(lz)"
print "  stress_tensor_polymer/solvent_*.dat and stress_profile_z_*_*.dat now"
print "  contain 3 equilibrated stages (appended) — fit ΔP′_net vs ε_vol"
print "  across them (plus the ε_vol=0 origin) for the slope = K."
print "========================================"

variable outfile string "final_compress_${dataname}_${interaction}_${nsteps}"
write_data ${outfile}.data
